  abstract = {{\textexclamdown}div class="abstract" data-abstract-type="normal"{\textquestiondown}{\textexclamdown}p{\textquestiondown}The methods of solution of the wave equation for a central field given in the previous paper are applied to various atoms. For the core electrons, the details of the interaction of the electrons in a single {\textexclamdown}span class='italic'{\textquestiondown}n{\textexclamdown}span class='sub'{\textquestiondown}k{\textexclamdown}/span{\textquestiondown}{\textexclamdown}/span{\textquestiondown} group are neglected, but an approximate correction is made for the fact that the distributed charge of an electron does not contribute to the field acting on itself (2).{\textexclamdown}/p{\textquestiondown}{\textexclamdown}p{\textquestiondown}For a given atom the object of the work is to find a field such that the solutions of the wave equation for the core electrons in this field (corrected as just mentioned for each core electron) give a distribution of charge which reproduces the field. This is called the self-consistent field, and the process of finding it is one of successive approximation ( 3).{\textexclamdown}/p{\textquestiondown}{\textexclamdown}p{\textquestiondown}Approximations to the self-consistent field have been found for He ( 4), Rb{\textexclamdown}span class='sup'{\textquestiondown}+{\textexclamdown}/span{\textquestiondown} ( 5), Na{\textexclamdown}span class='sup'{\textquestiondown}+{\textexclamdown}/span{\textquestiondown}, Cl{\textexclamdown}span class='sup'{\textquestiondown}-{\textexclamdown}/span{\textquestiondown} ( 9). For He the energy parameter for the solution of the wave equation for one electron in the self-consistent field of the nucleus and the other corresponds to an ionisation potential of 24{$\cdot$}85 volts (observed 24{$\cdot$}6 volts); this agreement suggests that for other atoms the values of the energy parameter in the self-consistent field (corrected for each core electron) will probably give good approximations to the X-ray terms (4).{\textexclamdown}/p{\textquestiondown}{\textexclamdown}p{\textquestiondown}The most extensive work has been carried out for Rb{\textexclamdown}span class='sup'{\textquestiondown}+{\textexclamdown}/span{\textquestiondown}. The distribution of charge given by the wave functions in the self-consistent field is compared with the distribution calculated by other methods ( 6). The values of X-ray and optical terms calculated from the self-consistent field show satisfactory agreement with those observed ( 7).{\textexclamdown}/p{\textquestiondown}{\textexclamdown}p{\textquestiondown}The wave mechanical analogue of the case in which on the orbital model an internal and an external orbit of the same energy are possible is discussed ( 8).{\textexclamdown}/p{\textquestiondown}{\textexclamdown}/div{\textquestiondown}},
  date-added = {2019-06-16T05:00:37GMT},
  date-modified = {2019-12-29T22:17:18GMT},
