  abstract = {We present an implementation of pair natural orbital second-order M{\o}ller--Plesset perturbation theory with computational costs that scale only cubically with the system size. The low cost-scaling is achieved by combining a hybrid approach, where the pair natural orbitals are build from orbital-specific virtuals OSVs, with an iterative block Davidson algorithm for solving the equations for OSVs. We thereby avoid a complete diagonalisation of amplitude matrices and the explicit construction of the corresponding exchange integral matrices. This reduces the cost-scaling for the generation of the OSVs and of the pair natural orbitals to without a priori assumptions about locality. The costs can be further reduced by combining the approach with a local resolution-of-the-identity approximation for the exchange integrals. The errors introduced by these approximations are negligible and do not affect the final accuracy of the correlation energy. Test calculations on a set of organic and inorganic molecules demonstr...},
