  url = {https://aip.scitation.org/doi/abs/10.1063/1.4820557},
  abstract = {We establish a formal connection between the particle-particle (pp) random phase approximation (RPA) and the ladder channel of the coupled cluster doubles (CCD) equations. The relationship between RPA and CCD is best understood within a Bogoliubov quasiparticle (qp) RPA formalism. This work is a follow-up to our previous formal proof on the connection between particle-hole (ph) RPA and ring-CCD. Whereas RPA is a quasibosonic approximation, CC theory is a ``correct bosonization'' in the sense that the wavefunction and Hilbert space are exactly fermionic, yet the amplitude equations can be interpreted as adding different quasibosonic RPA channels together. Coupled cluster theory achieves this goal by interacting the ph (ring) and pp (ladder) diagrams via a third channel that we here call ``crossed-ring'' whose presence allows for full fermionic antisymmetry. Additionally, coupled cluster incorporates what we call ``mosaic'' terms which can be absorbed into defining a new effective one-body Hamiltonian. The inclus...},
