  urldate = {2021-12-08},
  abstract = {It is shown that the many-electron wave function can be expanded optimally in terms of a set of slater determinants that reduces considerbly the number of determinats differing by a single-particle wave function. The method is based on a variational procedure. The first step of the present method is the Brueckner optimization. The other determinants of the expansion are obtained by successive optimizations performed under additional constraints. The method is illustrated by specifically three-and four particle example. Finally, it is concluded that the eigenstates of a many- particle system can be approximated by states that neglect single-particle excitations. The Zero-order approximation of the present scheme is the Hartree--Fock approximation.},
